Professor BIT proposes the following version of binary search:

bsearch(L,i,j,key) {
  if(i>j) return -1;
  k=(i+j)/2;
  if(key==L[k]) return k;
  if(key<L[k]) return bsearch(L,i,k,key);
  else return bsearch(L,k+1,j,key);
}

Is the professor’s version correct? Justify your answer and find its time complexity.
